**Plan, no changes made.**

`buildRows()` already returns full rows, `owner` and `slow` included. `toTable()` in [format.js](src/format.js) drops those two on purpose, by comment, for the text view.

```js
// cli.js
function main(argv) {
  const command = argv[0];
  const jsonFlag = argv.includes('--json');
  if (command !== 'report') { ... }
  const rows = buildRows();
  process.stdout.write((jsonFlag ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
  return 0;
}
```

JSON output keeps all fields since it isn't width-constrained like the table. Update `USAGE` to mention `--json`.

